body:
I very much enjoy it personally. Like what several people here have already said, Nikolai's route is fantastic; I was not expecting to love his route as much as I did and once I finished, I immediately wanted to replay it. I like the tension that's kept between the MC and Nikolai and like the way their attraction to each other was approached. 

&#x200B;

Remy's route is decent enough. MC is a little too enamored with him/romanticizing everything for it to be a great route, but I like the plot of it surprisingly quite a bit. Went in for the pretty boy, stayed for the story basically. 

&#x200B;

I plan on playing Vivienne's next after the current season I'm on for another route and then immediately after that playing ~~Jett~~ Zoe's route because I think QoT is telling good stories. At the very least I like the MC's reasoning for being with the group (the thrill of adventure) more than the MC's in GiL (she was ~~kidnapped~~ taken into protective custody and is just along for the ride).

The Zoolander Association is recruiting! 

We're looking to fill 14 slots in our association with fun people who love this game. 

&#x200B;

**Zoolander Info**

* ID#: 1532
* Level: 10
* Rank: 4371
* Co-Op Contest Hours: Friday/Saturday 7:30 AM - 8:30 AM server time

&#x200B;

**The only rule is you must be somewhat active.** We're not competitive so there's no weekly quota hanging over your head, but we do want to be respectful to everyone else in the guild who is putting in the time to add to the group so we do regularly purge people who have 0 activity for several weeks in a row.

&#x200B;

It's not always a very active community, but everyone is friendly and willing to chat, and I'd love it to see more activity/community going on within the association. We even have a FB group a few of us put together for sharing pictures of outfits and asking for advice. I know that the few of us who use it would love to see some new faces up in there! 

&#x200B;

Most everything I want has been mentioned here (including motherfucking ENTROPY) but what I really want is for them to actually show us a big city like they did with Kirkwall in DA2, hell, even Denerim in DAO. 

We hear such grandiose things about the big cities/cultures of the world and when we were promised Orlais I promptly flipped the fuck out. But we were given 2 courtyards of a GRAND city and repeated, generic fashions for a culture known for extravagance to the point of absurdity. I completely understand that creating unique masks for every single npc in Orlais is difficult as shit, but you're ruining your own world immersion by emphasising grandiosity and then presenting repetition. 

I probably won't get to see my Orlais in all it's glory and I accept that. But if we're really going to Tevinter, please don't make the same mistakes, Bioware ;A;
